prompt.text:
Repair the complete CommonJS source below. `moveCursor(entries, currentIndex, displacement)` models movement through an ordered history. `entries` must be an array of strings and may be empty. `currentIndex` must be `-1` for an empty array, or a valid index for a non-empty array. `displacement` must be an integer: negative values move toward earlier entries, positive values toward later entries, and zero stays put.

Movement beyond either boundary must clamp to the first or last entry. For an empty array return `{ index: -1, value: null }`. Otherwise return the clamped index and corresponding string. Do not mutate or copy `entries`. Malformed arguments throw `TypeError`, except an index inconsistent with the array throws `RangeError`. Export exactly `{ moveCursor }`.

Correct and return the entire source file:

```javascript
'use strict';

function moveCursor(entries, currentIndex, displacement) {
  if (!Array.isArray(entries) || entries.some(function (entry) { return typeof entry !== 'string'; })) {
    throw new TypeError('entries must be an array of strings');
  }
  if (!Number.isInteger(currentIndex)) throw new TypeError('currentIndex must be an integer');
  if (!Number.isInteger(displacement)) throw new TypeError('displacement must be an integer');
  if (entries.length === 0) {
    if (currentIndex !== -1) throw new RangeError('empty history requires index -1');
    return { index: -1, value: null };
  }
  if (currentIndex < 0 || currentIndex >= entries.length) {
    throw new RangeError('currentIndex is outside the history');
  }

  const index = Math.max(0, Math.min(entries.length - 1, currentIndex - displacement));
  return { index, value: entries[index] };
}

module.exports = { moveCursor };
```

